#: ../../library/turtle.rst:3
msgid ":mod:`!turtle` --- Turtle graphics"
msgstr ":mod:`!turtle` --- Grafika żółwia"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:10
msgid "**Source code:** :source:`Lib/turtle.py`"
msgstr "**Kod źródłowy:** :source:`Lib/turtle.py`"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:22
msgid ""
"Turtle can draw intricate shapes using programs that repeat simple moves."
msgstr ""
"Żółw może rysować skomplikowane kształty za pomocą programów, które "
"powtarzają proste ruchy."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:25
msgid "A yellow starburst of thin spikes with a red outline, drawn by turtle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:29
msgid ""
"Imagine a robotic turtle starting at (0, 0) in the x-y plane. After an "
"``import turtle``, give it the command ``turtle.forward(15)``, and it moves "
"(on-screen!) 15 pixels in the direction it is facing, drawing a line as it "
"moves. Give it the command ``turtle.right(25)``, and it rotates in-place 25 "
"degrees clockwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:35
msgid ""
"Turtle graphics is an implementation of `the drawing tools introduced in "
"Logo <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turtle_(robot)>`__ in 1967. It was "
"created as an educational tool, and its instant, visible feedback makes it "
"an effective way for learners to encounter programming concepts. It is also "
"a convenient way to produce simple graphical output without bringing in "
"external libraries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:41
msgid "This document includes four main sections:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:43
msgid ":ref:`turtle-tutorial` teaches the basics of turtle drawing."
msgstr ":ref:`turtle-tutorial` uczy podstawy rysowania."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:44
msgid ""
":ref:`turtle-reference` describes the functions, methods and classes this "
"module defines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:46
msgid ":ref:`turtle-howtos` detail how to handle specific tasks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:47
msgid ""
":ref:`turtle-explanation` provides background on the object-oriented "
"interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:52
msgid ""
"Turtle graphics requires the :mod:`tkinter` optional module. The python.org "
"installers for Windows and macOS include it, but some Linux distributions "
"and other platforms may package it separately. If ``import turtle`` fails "
"with an error mentioning ``_tkinter``, look for documentation from your "
"distributor (that is, whoever provided Python to you). Check this in advance "
"if you're planning to use turtle graphics with a learner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:65
msgid "Tutorial"
msgstr "Tutorial"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:67
msgid ""
"New users should start here. In this tutorial we'll explore some of the "
"basics of turtle drawing."
msgstr ""
"Nowi użytkownicy powinni zacząć tutaj. W tym tutorialu poznamy niektóre z "
"podstaw rysowania żółwi."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:72
msgid "Starting a turtle environment"
msgstr "Uruchamianie środowiska żółwia"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:74
msgid "In a Python shell, import all the objects of the ``turtle`` module::"
msgstr "W powłoce Pythona zaimportuj wszystkie obiekty z modułu ``turtle``::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:76
msgid "from turtle import *"
msgstr "from turtle import *"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:78
msgid ""
"If you run into a ``No module named '_tkinter'`` error, you'll have to "
"install the :mod:`Tk interface package <tkinter>` on your system."
msgstr ""
"Jeśli napotkasz błąd ``No module named '_tkinter'``, będziesz musiał "
"zainstalować :mod:`pakiet interfejsu Tk <tkinter>` w swoim systemie."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:83
msgid "Basic drawing"
msgstr "Podstawowe rysowanie"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:85
msgid "Send the turtle forward 100 steps::"
msgstr "Wyślij żółwia do przodu o 100 kroków:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:87
msgid "forward(100)"
msgstr "forward(100)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:89
msgid ""
"You should see (most likely, in a new window on your display) a line drawn "
"by the turtle, heading East. Change the direction of the turtle, so that it "
"turns 120 degrees left (anti-clockwise)::"
msgstr ""
"Powinieneś zobaczyć (najprawdopodobniej w nowym oknie na ekranie) linię "
"narysowaną przez żółwia w kierunku wschodnim. Zmień kierunek żółwia, tak aby "
"obrócił się o 120 stopni w lewo (przeciwnie do ruchu wskazówek zegara)::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:93
msgid "left(120)"
msgstr "left(120)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:95
msgid "Let's continue by drawing a triangle::"
msgstr "Kontynuujmy, rysując trójkąt::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:97
msgid ""
"forward(100)\n"
"left(120)\n"
"forward(100)"
msgstr ""
"forward(100)\n"
"left(120)\n"
"forward(100)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:101
msgid ""
"Notice how the turtle, represented by an arrow, points in different "
"directions as you steer it."
msgstr ""
"Zwróć uwagę, jak żółw, reprezentowany przez strzałkę, kieruje się w różnych "
"kierunkach."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:104
msgid ""
"Experiment with those commands, and also with ``backward()`` and "
"``right()``. Many commands also have shorter aliases, such as ``fd()`` for :"
"func:`forward`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:110 ../../library/turtle.rst:797
msgid "Pen control"
msgstr "Kontrola pióra"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:112
msgid ""
"Try changing the color - for example, ``color('blue')`` - and width of the "
"line - for example, ``width(3)`` - and then drawing again."
msgstr ""
"Spróbuj zmienić kolor – na przykład ``color('blue')`` – i szerokość linii – "
"na przykład ``width(3)`` – a następnie narysuj ponownie."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:115
msgid ""
"You can also move the turtle around without drawing, by lifting up the pen: "
"``up()`` before moving. To start drawing again, use ``down()``."
msgstr ""
"Żółwia można także przesuwać bez rysowania, podnosząc pióro: ``up()`` przed "
"wykonaniem ruchu. Aby ponownie rozpocząć rysowanie, użyj ``down()``."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:120
msgid "The turtle's position"
msgstr "Pozycja żółwia"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:122
msgid ""
"Send your turtle back to its starting-point (useful if it has disappeared "
"off-screen)::"
msgstr ""
"Wyślij żółwia z powrotem do punktu początkowego (przydatne, jeśli zniknął "
"poza ekranem)::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:125
msgid "home()"
msgstr "home()"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:127
msgid ""
"The home position is at the center of the turtle's screen. If you ever need "
"to know them, get the turtle's x-y coordinates with::"
msgstr ""
"Pozycja wyjściowa znajduje się na środku ekranu żółwia. Jeśli kiedykolwiek "
"będziesz chciał(a) je poznać, uzyskaj współrzędne x-y żółwia za pomocą::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:130
msgid "pos()"
msgstr "pos()"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:132
msgid "Home is at ``(0, 0)``."
msgstr "Pozycja wyjściowa znajduje się pod ``(0, 0)``."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:134
msgid ""
"And after a while, it will probably help to clear the window so we can start "
"anew::"
msgstr ""
"A po pewnym czasie prawdopodobnie przyda się wyczyścić okno, abyśmy mogli "
"zacząć od nowa::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:137
msgid "clearscreen()"
msgstr "clearscreen()"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:141
msgid "Making algorithmic patterns"
msgstr "Tworzenie wzorców algorytmicznych"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:143
msgid "Using loops, it's possible to build up geometric patterns::"
msgstr "Za pomocą pętli można tworzyć geometryczne wzory::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:145
msgid ""
"for steps in range(100):\n"
"    for c in ('blue', 'red', 'green'):\n"
"        color(c)\n"
"        forward(steps)\n"
"        right(30)"
msgstr ""
"for steps in range(100):\n"
"    for c in ('blue', 'red', 'green'):\n"
"        color(c)\n"
"        forward(steps)\n"
"        right(30)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:152
msgid "\\ - which of course, are limited only by the imagination!"
msgstr "– które oczywiście ogranicza tylko wyobraźnia!"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:154
msgid ""
"Let's draw the star shape at the top of this page. We want red lines, filled "
"in with yellow::"
msgstr ""
"Narysujmy kształt gwiazdy z góry tej strony. Potrzebujemy czerwonych linii, "
"wypełnionych kolorem żółtym::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:157
msgid ""
"color('red')\n"
"fillcolor('yellow')"
msgstr ""
"color('red')\n"
"fillcolor('yellow')"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:160
msgid ""
"Just as ``up()`` and ``down()`` determine whether lines will be drawn, "
"filling can be turned on and off::"
msgstr ""
"Podobnie jak ``up()`` i ``down()`` określają, czy linie będą rysowane, "
"wypełnianie można włączać i wyłączać::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:163
msgid "begin_fill()"
msgstr "begin_fill()"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:165
msgid "Next we'll create a loop::"
msgstr "Następnie utworzymy pętlę::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:167
msgid ""
"start = pos()\n"
"\n"
"while True:\n"
"    forward(200)\n"
"    left(170)\n"
"    if distance(start) < 1:\n"
"        break"
msgstr ""
"start = pos()\n"
"\n"
"while True:\n"
"    forward(200)\n"
"    left(170)\n"
"    if distance(start) < 1:\n"
"        break"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:175
msgid ""
"``distance(start) < 1`` is a good way to know when the turtle is back at its "
"start position."
msgstr ""
"``distance(start) < 1`` to dobry sposób, aby dowiedzieć się, kiedy żółw "
"powróci do pozycji startowej."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:178
msgid "Finally, complete the filling::"
msgstr "Na koniec uzupełnij wypełnienie::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:180
msgid "end_fill()"
msgstr "end_fill()"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:182
msgid ""
"(Note that filling only actually takes place when you give the "
"``end_fill()`` command.)"
msgstr ""
"(Należy pamiętać, że wypełnianie odbywa się tylko po wydaniu polecenia "
"``end_fill()``.)"

